      "dom_id": "question-70169",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$\\frac{5}{12}\\times 8=$",
      "worked_solution": "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 8}{12}=\\frac{40}{12}\n$$\n\nWe then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{40}{12}=\\frac{40÷4}{12÷4}=\\frac{10}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{10}{3}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n10÷3=3\\,\\text{R}1=3\\,\\frac{1}{3}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
